{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/240950-shadows-of-the-crusade","id":240950,"title":"Shadows of the Crusade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-25T19:19:39-07:00","id":240950,"title":"Shadows of the Crusade","content":"&quot;And we shall walk in the shadow of death, and know that death is not what you should fear.&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole concept of a campaign of mine that will be starting soon is a whole World of Darkness campaign during the events of the Third Crusade. The players are two Sin Eaters who will be traveling with two other Sin Eaters. The game begins the night before the taking of the city of Acre by King Richard's men during the Third Crusade.<br /> <br /> This game is slightly an experiment, messing around with Sin Eaters in pre-modern times. As well as sort of using all manner of other supernaturals and how any of them would connect with the events there in the Holy Land.<br /> <br /> I am curious if anyone would have any ideas about enemies the group could possibly make, allies, etc; during a campaign based in this period of history.<br /> As a note, I am completely open to bending the lore slightly, since so much of the lore is conjecture as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3762-brutalskars","name":"Brutalskars","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:24:56-07:00","id":241092,"title":"","content":"Depends on what type of game you want to run. Do you expect to run special forces type missions for the Crusades and have that be a thing? Do you plan on exploring the differences in culture? Doing a Knights Templar-like thing involving secret societies? Do you plan on presenting Muslims as the enemy or do you plan on bridging that gap? From your description, are they partaking in the Crusades at all or are they literally following in the aftermath of them?<br /> <br /> Crusades are a setting, and a potentially fruitful one. That doesn't tell anyone what type of game you plan on playing, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:34:09-07:00","id":241098,"title":"","content":"My idea as it stands is that they will most certainly come into friends and foes on both sides of the war. Not necessarily all of these friends and foes will be direct allies of the Muslims or the Christians; such as European supernaturals who have come to the Middle East to steal artifacts, take advantage of the chaos and such - as well as those who would want to stop potential crisis arising from the conflict at hand. As well as mirrored ideals of some form in the Muslim and more native forces.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of them coming and going through the aftermath and participating as they see fit. I also do like the idea of secret societies, such as the knightly orders and beyond - even possibly tapping into some possible very ancient Hunter Traditions which would most certainly be a threat to any supernatural beings participating in the conflict.<br /> I want to explore the secret, supernatural side of the war that could of existed.<br /> Even if it would mean having to tap into enemies I have never seen used in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3762-brutalskars","name":"Brutalskars","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:46:27-07:00","id":244012,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, the Knights Templar were destroyed based on the false claims they had founded some sort of cult in Jerusalem. Maybe that could become a Krewe or Hunter Conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T09:44:35-07:00","id":244084,"title":"","content":"Vampire: the Requiem's &quot;Ancient Mysteries/Ancient Bloodlines&quot; has a chapter on the Kindred of both sides during the Crusades. Worth looking into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T13:10:05-07:00","id":244290,"title":"","content":"So, third crusade. Europe was more/less successful-&quot;ish&quot;, but didn't manage to take Jerusalem. The Sin Eaters are presumably European in look and descent. Sure the Crusades are done, but the Relics that the shadowy overlords created the Crusades the get close to are still where they are. Now its time for the *real* war to begin. Start them off entering one of the cities flipped by the Crusades. Emphasize the impact of the war and the near global disdain for them because they are european.<br /> <br /> The mood in the world around them should be desperation. A question you'll have to answer is whether the PCs are meant to share that mood, or experience it from a point of privledge. I like the latter for a game, since its more fun and gives you something to threaten later. If your doing a Crusades game, you also basically have to put some epic prize in Jerusalem, even if the PCs don't know about it yet.<br /> <br /> The PCs should be in this city with an extremely specific purpose, even if you plan on running the game almost purely sandbox. That will set a tone and give the game direction. While they are participating in the story, through NPCs, they need to get caught up in Other Stuff(tm). What that other stuff looks like will depend on the PC's personalities and the goals they have set up for their character. You have indiana jones? Have them find the location to relics. You have a hardcore Pilgrim? Emphasize the ghosts left in the wake of the war. They're still fighting. You're not sure if they'll ever stop. Etc. Etc. Etc.<br /> <br /> And remember. The whole world revolves around Jerusalem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}